# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/tailoring-enchanting
title Tailoring + Enchanting 1-300
category Professions
kind profession
skills Tailoring, Enchanting
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Tailoring and Enchanting 1-300 together, for both factions: neither needs a gathering profession.
# Each rank bracket levels Tailoring first, then Enchanting, and the green armour Tailoring made in
# the bracket is disenchanted for Enchanting's dust and essences. The Enchanting steps say how much
# of what they ask your own crafts give; the rest comes from greens you loot or the Auction House
# (Gather, Buy or Mix).
#
# What disenchanting gives is Forever's server data for green armour of each item level, and the
# item levels the client's; the item level bands and the Enchanting skill disenchanting asks are
# Classic's (ASSUMED). Over the route your own crafts give about 489 enchanting materials against
# the 621 the Enchanting steps ask for.
#
# Tailoring:
# Tailoring sews cloth into bolts and the bolts into cloth armour, bags and shirts. It needs no
# gathering profession: humanoids drop the cloth of their level as you quest. Thread and dyes come
# from tailoring and trade supplies vendors.
#
# Forever's changes: nearly every pattern moved 25 points down: trainers teach it 25 points earlier
# (Bolt of Silk Cloth at 100, Gloves of Meditation at 105) and it greys sooner. Forever adds school
# sets (sashes, slippers, belts and more), reagent bags, and the Faction Banner camp item. 74
# patterns need a Spinning Wheel, a camp station (skill 140) from a blueprint the Unstable Sentinel
# drops in the City of Dalaran; 43 more need the skill-300 Loom (no known source); Mooncloth needs a
# Moonwell. New patterns are also sold for Merchant's Favor by Jim'bek near the Crossroads and Mivin
# Shadowweave at Three Corners (Redridge). Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply crates
# turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind when picked up. Tailoring has no
# specialisation on Forever.
#
# Ranks: Journeyman needs character level 10 (Forever's sniffed lists). Trainers teach by tier and
# train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at
# Georgio Bolero (Stormwind), Charles Worth (Alterac Mountains: Forever's own trainer, Alliance,
# seen training Expert in players' recordings) and Josef Gregorian (Undercity), from 125; Artisan
# only at Timothy Worthington (Theramore, Dustwallow Marsh) and Daryl Stack (Tarren Mill,
# Hillsbrad), from 200.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-15  Bolt of Linen Cloth, about 14 (known): 2 Linen Cloth each
#    15-55  Linen Belt, about 41 (trainer 50c): 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread each
#    55-75  Bolt of Woolen Cloth, about 21 (trainer 1s): 3 Wool Cloth each
#    75-100 Woolen Cape, about 34 (trainer 2s 50c): 1 Bolt of Woolen Cloth and 1 Fine Thread each
#   100-120 Bolt of Silk Cloth, about 40 (trainer 5s): 4 Silk Cloth each
#   120-135 Azure Silk Hood, about 17 (trainer 6s): 2 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Blue Dye and 1 Fine Thread each
#   135-150 Formal White Shirt, about 17 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Bleach and 1 Fine Thread each
#   150-170 Azure Silk Cloak, about 22 (recipe 15s): 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Blue Dye and 2 Fine Thread each
#   170-200 Black Mageweave Vest, about 36 (trainer): 2 Bolt of Mageweave and 3 Silken Thread each
#   200-225 Black Mageweave Headband, about 37 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Mageweave and 2 Heavy Silken Thread each
#   225-234 Runecloth Belt, about 11 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Runecloth and 1 Rune Thread each
#   234-265 Runecloth Gloves, about 43 (recipe 1g 60s): 4 Bolt of Runecloth, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread each
#   265-300 Runecloth Shoulders, about 62 (pattern from the Auction House): 7 Bolt of Runecloth, 2 Ironweb Spider Silk, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread each
#   without the pattern:
#     265-280 Runecloth Boots, about 100 (recipe 2g): 4 Bolt of Runecloth, 2 Ironweb Spider Silk, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread each
#     280-300 no trainer or vendor recipe gives points without a camp station (see the last step)
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count, enough for 9 players in 10):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 1s 50c, vendor goods 4s 10c; gather or buy 84 Linen Cloth and 69
# Wool Cloth.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s, recipes 13s 50c plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 93s 50c; gather
# or buy 57 Wool Cloth and 424 Silk Cloth.
# 150-225: recipes 15s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 20g 86s; gather or buy 300 Silk
# Cloth and 1060 Mageweave Cloth.
# 225-300: recipes 1g 60s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 27g; gather or buy 200 Rugged
# Leather and 1195 Runecloth.
# 265-300 (with Pattern: Runecloth Shoulders): vendor goods 31g; gather or buy 296 Rugged Leather,
# 2590 Runecloth and 148 Ironweb Spider Silk.
# 265-300 (without the pattern): recipes 2g, vendor goods 50g; gather or buy 588 Rugged Leather,
# 2940 Runecloth and 294 Ironweb Spider Silk.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# Learn skills players' recordings bear out (estimated from Classic's lists; the lowest skill
# players learned each at, never below): Formal White Shirt 135 (22 players), Bolt of Mageweave 140
# (31 players), Black Mageweave Vest 170 (9 players), Bolt of Runecloth 205 (6 players) and
# Runecloth Belt 210 (3 players).
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed lists ask level 1
# for Apprentice and 10 for Journeyman). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
#
# Enchanting:
# Enchanting turns magic items into enchanting materials (Disenchant: any green or better item gives
# dust, essence or a shard by its level) and puts enchantments on gear. It needs no gathering
# profession: the dust and essence come from disenchanting what you loot, or from the Auction House.
# Each tier needs a runed rod in your bags (Copper, Silver, Golden, Truesilver, Arcanite); the rod
# bases come from blacksmiths or trade vendors.
#
# Forever's changes: the first levels run on Mote of Magic, 10c at enchanting supply vendors with no
# stock limit. Runed Copper Rod is a Copper Rod and 1 Mote; Bracer - Inferior Stamina (Classic's
# Minor Health) takes 1 Mote and goes grey at 25; Dust to Motes turns 1 Strange Dust into 3 Motes.
# Strange Dust and Lesser Magic Essence are still sold, but only 1 to 4 at a time, so this route
# runs on the Strange Dust that low-level greens break into (Chest - Inferior Stamina, then Cloak -
# Minor Protection). Several later formulas need fewer materials (Runed Silver Rod: 3 Strange Dust
# and 4 Lesser Magic Essence). New formulas for caster weapons, relics and necklaces are sold for
# Merchant's Favor by Beneris near the Crossroads. Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply
# crates turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind when picked up.
#
# Camping: Enchanted Lute (skill 20) is the Enchanting camp item. The Arcane Salvager (skill 140,
# blueprint from Rath'mael, Ruins of Lordaeron) improves disenchanting at a camp and needs the Runed
# Truesilver Rod; the skill-300 Arcane Forge has no known blueprint source.
#
# Ranks: trainers teach by tier and train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city
# trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at Kitta Firewind (Tower of Azora, Elwynn Forest) and Hgarth
# (Sun Rock Retreat, Stonetalon Mountains), from 125. Artisan is taught only by Annora inside
# Uldaman: enter by the back door (Badlands), clear the scorpids in her room until she appears, and
# learn every formula up to 250 on that visit. The new starter quests An Enchanting Lesson (Kitta
# Firewind, Alliance) and A Pain in the Neck (Pa'zula, Sen'jin Village, Horde) teach Disenchant on a
# quest item. Enchanting has no specialisation.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-25  Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina, about 31 (known): 1 Mote of Magic each
#    25-75  Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, about 51 (trainer 50c): 1 Strange Dust each
#    75-90  Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, about 22 (trainer 50c): 1 Strange Dust each
#    90-130 Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection, about 48 (trainer 2s): 2 Strange Dust each
#   130-150 Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina, about 20 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   150-160 Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina, about 11 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   160-195 Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility, about 39 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   195-205 Enchant Chest - Greater Intellect, about 10 (trainer): 1 Lesser Mystic Essence each
#   205-225 Enchant Cloak - Greater Defense, about 20 (trainer): 1 Vision Dust each
#   225-253 Enchant Gloves - Agility, about 39 (trainer): 1 Vision Dust each
#   253-275 Lesser Mana Oil, about 34 (recipe 1g): 1 Dream Dust, 1 Purple Lotus and 1 Crystal Vial each
#   275-300 Enchant Shield - Greater Stamina, about 29 (recipe 1g 20s): 6 Dream Dust each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count, enough for 9 players in 10):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 50c, vendor goods 4s 44c; gather or buy 52 Strange Dust.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s (Classic price), recipes 2s plus unpriced trainer recipes; gather or buy 1
# Shadowgem, 1 Silver Rod, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 136 Strange Dust and 20 Soul Dust.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), trainer recipes (prices not in the data); gather or buy 1
# Iridescent Pearl, 1 Black Pearl, 1 Greater Astral Essence, 55 Soul Dust, 1 Golden Rod, 10 Lesser
# Mystic Essence, 1 Greater Mystic Essence, 21 Vision Dust and 1 Truesilver Rod.
# 225-300: Artisan 5g (Classic price), recipes 2g 20s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 1g
# 70s; gather or buy 41 Purple Lotus, 45 Vision Dust and 233 Dream Dust.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# Learn skills players' recordings bear out (estimated from Classic's lists; the lowest skill
# players learned each at, never below): Runed Silver Rod 100 (41 players), Enchant Bracer - Lesser
# Stamina 130 (21 players), Runed Golden Rod 150 (19 players), Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility 160
# (11 players), Enchant Chest - Greater Intellect 185 (10 players), Runed Truesilver Rod 200 (10
# players) and Enchant Cloak - Greater Defense 205 (7 players).
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Enchant Gloves - Agility 210 (no sniffed Forever list teaches them:
# Classic's trainer skill moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which the sniffed
# lists bear out on 126 of 129 recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer asks; their prices are
# not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Journeyman 10, Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed
# lists ask level 1 for Apprentice). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Journeyman 5s, Expert 50s and Artisan 5g (Classic's trainer lists; Forever's
# sniffed lists price only Apprentice, 10c as in Classic). In-game check: what each rank costs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Tailoring 1-75

step Learn Tailoring
  tip Apprentice Tailoring lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Any Tailoring trainer of your faction teaches it; the arrow picks the nearest. Keep every Linen Cloth you loot: humanoids of level 5-20 drop it. 1-75 takes about 1s 50c of recipes and 4s 10c of vendor goods, plus 84 Linen Cloth and 69 Wool Cloth to gather or buy.
  train Tailoring Apprentice
  skill Tailoring 1

step Tailoring 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 41 Coarse Thread (4s 10c); about 4s 10c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2320 x41 nearest

step Get Linen Cloth
  tip 84 Linen Cloth for Tailoring 1-75: 14 Bolts of Linen Cloth and 42 Linen Belts. Humanoids of level 5-20 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Linen Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2589 x84 nearest gather levels 5-20
  auction 2589 x84

step Get Wool Cloth
  tip 69 Wool Cloth for Tailoring 1-75: 23 Bolts of Woolen Cloth. Humanoids of level 15-30 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Wool Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2592 x69 nearest gather levels 15-30
  auction 2592 x69

step Bolt of Linen Cloth to 15
  tip Bolt of Linen Cloth is orange at 1 (yellow 25, green 37, grey 50): about 14 crafts to 15, a point every craft. Each takes 2 Linen Cloth. Keep the bolts: the Linen Belts from 15 take one each.
  craft 2963 until 15

step Tailoring recipes at 15
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Linen Belt (from 15, 50c).
  learn 8776

step Linen Belt to 55
  tip Linen Belt is orange at 15 (yellow 50, green 67, grey 85): about 41 crafts to 55, up to 42 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread. Make the 27 Bolt of Linen Cloth first: it gives points too while not grey. Use the 14 Bolt of Linen Cloth you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Each belt takes one bolt; the belts sell to vendors.
  craft 2963 x27
  craft 8776 until 55

step Tailoring recipes at 55
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Bolt of Woolen Cloth (from 55, 1s). Also learn Faction Banner (1s): Forever's Tailoring camp item, a Bolt of Linen Cloth and a Coarse Thread; each faction has its own. The Camping 101: Tailoring quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to a tailoring trainer who teaches it free.
  learn 2964
  learn 1263425 only Alliance
  learn 1229504 only Horde

step Bolt of Woolen Cloth to 75
  tip Bolt of Woolen Cloth is orange at 55 (yellow 70, green 77, grey 85): about 21 crafts to 75, up to 23 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 3 Wool Cloth. Keep the bolts: the Woolen Capes from 75 take one each, so these points cost no extra Wool Cloth.
  craft 2964 until 75
  skill Tailoring 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Enchanting 1-75

step Learn Enchanting
  tip Apprentice Enchanting lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Not every Enchanting trainer teaches it: Alliance Alanna Raveneye (Teldrassil), Betty Quin (Stormwind City), Eaysaa Brightgust (Zephras Isle), Lalina Summermoon (Darnassus), Nasalanna Windsinger (Zephras Isle) and Thonys Pillarstone (Ironforge); Horde Eaysaa Brightgust (Zephras Isle), Jhag (Orgrimmar), Malcomb Wynn (Undercity), Mot Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff), Nasalanna Windsinger (Zephras Isle), Pa'zula (Durotar) and Vance Undergloom (Tirisfal Glades). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Buy a Copper Rod and Mote of Magic from an enchanting supplies vendor (in the capitals and on Zephras Isle; the starting-area trainers have none beside them, and the next step's arrow picks the nearest). From now on, disenchant every green you do not wear: that is where the dust and essences come from. Two starter quests teach Disenchant on a quest item: An Enchanting Lesson from Kitta Firewind (Tower of Azora, Elwynn Forest) and A Pain in the Neck from Pa'zula (Sen'jin Village, Durotar). 1-75 takes about 50c of recipes and 4s 44c of vendor goods, plus 52 Strange Dust to gather or buy.
  train Enchanting Apprentice
  skill Enchanting 1

step Enchanting 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 1 Copper Rod (1s 24c) and 32 Mote of Magic (3s 20c); about 4s 44c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Jessara Cordell; Orgrimmar: Kithas).
  buy 6217 x1 nearest
  buy 247786 x32 nearest

step Get Strange Dust
  tip 52 Strange Dust for Enchanting 1-75: 52 Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina. Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-20. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 10940 x52 anywhere gather Enchanting 1
  auction 10940 x52

step Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina to 25
  tip Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina is orange at 1 (yellow 20, green 22, grey 25): about 31 crafts to 25, up to 38 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Mote of Magic. One Mote of Magic (10c) a craft; grey at 25 on Forever. Make the Runed Copper Rod first: the recipe needs it in your bags, so keep it there. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7421 x1 -- a tool: keep it in your bags
  craft 7418 until 25

step Enchanting recipes at 25
  tip Back to an Enchanting trainer: Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina (from 15, 50c). Also learn Enchanted Lute (1s): Forever's Enchanting camp item, 1 Simple Wood and 1 Strange Dust, placed at a campsite beside a campfire for its buff. The Camping 101: Enchanting quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to an enchanting trainer who teaches it free.
  learn 7420
  learn 1230643

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina to 75
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina is orange at 25 (yellow 70, green 90, grey 110): about 51 crafts to 75, up to 52 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Strange Dust. One Strange Dust a craft: the dust most level 5-20 greens break into, armour above all. Lesser Magic Essence (from weapons) does the same job through Bracer - Minor Deflect or Chest - Minor Absorption if you have more of it. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7420 until 75
  skill Enchanting 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman (75-150)
section Tailoring 75-150

step Journeyman Tailoring
  tip Journeyman raises the cap from 75 to 150 for 5s; it needs Tailoring 50 and character level 10, so you can take it on any visit from 50. Not every Tailoring trainer teaches it: Alliance Charles Worth (Alterac Mountains), Grarnik Goodstitch (Stranglethorn Vale), Jormund Stonebrow (Ironforge), Me'lynn (Darnassus), Othesia Evengale (Zephras Isle), Sellandus (Stormwind City) and Taleen Shimmerthread (Zephras Isle); Horde Grarnik Goodstitch (Stranglethorn Vale), Magar (Orgrimmar), Mahani (The Barrens), Othesia Evengale (Zephras Isle), Rhiannon Davis (Undercity), Taleen Shimmerthread (Zephras Isle) and Tepa (Thunder Bluff). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Woolen Cape (from 55, 2s 50c). 75-150 takes about 13s 50c of recipes and 93s 50c of vendor goods, plus 57 Wool Cloth and 424 Silk Cloth to gather or buy. Train Journeyman Enchanting on the same trip (it needs Enchanting 50 and character level 10; the arrow picks the nearest Enchanting trainer who teaches it): the Enchanting steps below need it.
  level 10
  train Tailoring Journeyman
  train Enchanting Journeyman
  learn 2402

step Tailoring 75-150: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 68 Fine Thread (68s), 34 Bleach (8s 50c) and 34 Blue Dye (17s); about 93s 50c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero and Edna Mullby; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2321 x68 nearest
  buy 2324 x34 nearest
  buy 6260 x34 nearest

step Get Wool Cloth
  tip 57 Wool Cloth for Tailoring 75-150: 40 Woolen Capes. Humanoids of level 15-30 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Wool Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2592 x57 nearest gather levels 15-30
  auction 2592 x57

step Get Silk Cloth
  tip 424 Silk Cloth for Tailoring 75-150: 55 Bolts of Silk Cloth and 19 Formal White Shirts. Humanoids of level 25-45 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Silk Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 4306 x424 nearest gather levels 25-45
  auction 4306 x424

step Woolen Cape to 100
  tip Woolen Cape is orange at 75 (yellow 80, green 97, grey 115): about 34 crafts to 100, up to 40 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Bolt of Woolen Cloth and 1 Fine Thread. Make the 13 Bolt of Woolen Cloth first: it gives points too while not grey. Use the 21 Bolt of Woolen Cloth you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. If you got here without learning Bolt of Woolen Cloth, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 2964
  craft 2964 x13
  craft 2402 until 100

step Tailoring recipes at 100
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Bolt of Silk Cloth (from 100, 5s).
  learn 3839

step Bolt of Silk Cloth to 120
  tip Bolt of Silk Cloth is orange at 100 (yellow 110, green 115, grey 120): about 40 crafts to 120, up to 55 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 4 Silk Cloth. Silk Cloth drops from humanoids of level 25-45. Keep every bolt: the hoods and shirts to 150 take them, so these points cost no extra Silk Cloth.
  craft 3839 until 120

step Tailoring recipes at 120
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Azure Silk Hood (from 120, 6s).
  learn 8760

step Azure Silk Hood to 135
  tip Azure Silk Hood is orange at 120 (yellow 130, green 135, grey 140): about 17 crafts to 135, up to 19 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Blue Dye and 1 Fine Thread. Use the 34 Bolt of Silk Cloth you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Two silk bolts and two Blue Dye a hood: orange to 130, a point every craft.
  craft 8760 until 135

step Tailoring recipes at 135
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Formal White Shirt (from 135).
  learn 3871

step Formal White Shirt to 150
  tip Formal White Shirt is orange at 135 (yellow 145, green 150, grey 155): about 17 crafts to 150, up to 19 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Bleach and 1 Fine Thread. Make the 45 Bolt of Silk Cloth first. Use the 6 Bolt of Silk Cloth you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Bleach from tailoring and trade supplies vendors. Tailoring 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3839 x45
  craft 3871 until 150
  skill Tailoring 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman (75-150)
section Enchanting 75-150

step Journeyman Enchanting
  tip Disenchant the green armour you made for Tailoring 75-150: 34 Woolen Capes and 17 Azure Silk Hoods (item level 29, from Enchanting 50) give about 64 Strange Dust, 19 Soul Dust, 10 Greater Magic Essence, 5 Greater Astral Essence and 2 Small Glimmering Shard. Journeyman raises the cap from 75 to 150 for 5s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Enchanting 50 and character level 10, so you can take it on any visit from 50. Not every Enchanting trainer teaches it: Alliance Gimble Thistlefuzz (Ironforge), Lucan Cordell (Stormwind City), Taladan (Darnassus) and Xylinnia Starshine (Feralas); Horde Godan (Orgrimmar), Lavinia Crowe (Undercity) and Teg Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection (from 70, 2s). 75-150 takes about 2s of recipes, plus 1 Shadowgem, 1 Silver Rod, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 136 Strange Dust and 20 Soul Dust to gather or buy.
  level 10
  train Enchanting Journeyman
  learn 7771

step Enchanting 75-150: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 4 Lesser Magic Essence (32s). The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction. Lesser Magic Essence: no vendor of the other faction sells it; that side gathers or buys it at the Auction House (next steps).
  buy 10938 x4 nearest only Horde

step Get Shadowgem
  tip 1 Shadowgem for Enchanting 75-150: Runed Silver Rod. Shadowgem turns up in about one Copper Vein, Tin Vein or Silver Vein in 100: keep the ones you find while mining. Or buy it at the Auction House.
  collect 1210 x1 anywhere gather Mining 1
  auction 1210 x1

step Get Silver Rod
  tip 1 Silver Rod for Enchanting 75-150: Runed Silver Rod. Blacksmithing: Silver Rod. Or buy it at the Auction House.
  collect 6338 x1 anywhere gather Blacksmithing 75
  auction 6338 x1

step Get Strange Dust
  tip 136 Strange Dust for Enchanting 75-150: 27 Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, 53 Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection and Runed Silver Rod. Disenchanting your Tailoring crafts of this bracket gives about 64 of them (see Journeyman Enchanting); the other 72 come from greens you loot or the Auction House. Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-20. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 10940 x136 anywhere gather Enchanting 1
  auction 10940 x136

step Get Soul Dust
  tip 20 Soul Dust for Enchanting 75-150: 20 Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina. Disenchanting your Tailoring crafts of this bracket gives about 19 of them (see Journeyman Enchanting); the other 1 come from greens you loot or the Auction House. Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 21-30. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 11083 x20 anywhere gather Enchanting 1
  auction 11083 x20

step Enchanting 75-150: Auction House
  tip What 75-150 takes that the Auction House sells and no step above farms: 4 Lesser Magic Essence. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 10938 x4 only Alliance

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina to 90
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina is yellow at 75 (yellow 70, green 90, grey 110): about 22 crafts to 90, up to 27 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Strange Dust. One Strange Dust a craft: the dust most level 5-20 greens break into, armour above all. Lesser Magic Essence (from weapons) does the same job through Bracer - Minor Deflect or Chest - Minor Absorption if you have more of it. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one. If you got here without learning Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 7420
  craft 7420 until 90

step Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection to 130
  tip Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection is orange at 90 (yellow 110, green 130, grey 150): about 48 crafts to 130, up to 53 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Strange Dust. Two Strange Dust a craft (the trainer teaches it from 70 for 2s); keep disenchanting the greens of the 10-20 zones. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7771 until 130

step Enchanting recipes at 130
  tip Back to an Enchanting trainer: Runed Silver Rod (from 100) and Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina (from 130).
  learn 7795
  learn 13501

step Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina to 150
  tip Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina is orange at 130 (yellow 155, green 175, grey 195): about 20 crafts to 150, a point every craft. Each takes 1 Soul Dust. One Soul Dust a craft (level 21-30 greens). Make the Runed Silver Rod first: the recipe needs it in your bags, so keep it there. Lesser Magic Essence (4 for 75-150): Alliance: Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-15; or the Auction House. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one. Enchanting 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 7795 x1 -- a tool: keep it in your bags
  craft 13501 until 150
  skill Enchanting 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert (150-225)
section Tailoring 150-225

step Tailoring 150-225: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 44 Fine Thread (44s), 108 Silken Thread (5g 40s), 44 Blue Dye (22s) and 74 Heavy Silken Thread (14g 80s); about 20g 86s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2321 x44 nearest
  buy 4291 x108 nearest
  buy 6260 x44 nearest
  buy 8343 x74 nearest

step Pattern: Azure Silk Cloak
  tip Pattern: Azure Silk Cloak teaches Azure Silk Cloak (Tailoring 140) for 15s. Sold by Alliance: Brienna Starglow (Feralas), limited stock and Norvin Alderman (Alterac Mountains); Horde: Jun'ha (Arathi Highlands), limited stock and Norvin Alderman (Alterac Mountains).
  buy 7089 nearest

step Get Silk Cloth
  tip 300 Silk Cloth for Tailoring 150-225: 25 Azure Silk Cloaks. Humanoids of level 25-45 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Silk Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 4306 x300 nearest gather levels 25-45
  auction 4306 x300

step Get Mageweave Cloth
  tip 1060 Mageweave Cloth for Tailoring 150-225: 40 Black Mageweave Vests and 44 Black Mageweave Headbands. Humanoids of level 35-50 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Mageweave Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 4338 x1060 nearest gather levels 35-50
  auction 4338 x1060

step Expert Tailoring
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225; it needs Tailoring 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Charles Worth (Alterac Mountains) and Georgio Bolero (Stormwind City); Horde Josef Gregorian (Undercity). This route trains it at Georgio Bolero (Stormwind City) for the Alliance and Josef Gregorian (Undercity) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 150-225: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Bolt of Mageweave (from 140). 150-225 takes about 15s of recipes and 20g 86s of vendor goods, plus 300 Silk Cloth and 1060 Mageweave Cloth to gather or buy. Come with all of it in your bags (the steps above, the rest from the Auction House): these trainers also teach Black Mageweave Vest (from 170), and the crafts need no station, so craft right here and learn each recipe as you reach its skill. One trip instead of 2. Black Mageweave Headband (from 200) takes a second trip, to other trainers (below).
  level 20
  train Tailoring Expert npc 1346 only Alliance
  train Tailoring Expert npc 4576 only Horde
  learn 3865 npc 1346 only Alliance
  learn 3865 npc 4576 only Horde

step Azure Silk Cloak to 170
  tip Azure Silk Cloak is orange at 150 (yellow 160, green 175, grey 190): about 22 crafts to 170, up to 25 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Blue Dye and 2 Fine Thread. Make the 66 Bolt of Silk Cloth first. Its recipe is the one bought above; it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. If you got here without learning Bolt of Silk Cloth, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 8786 -- from the recipe in your bags
  learn 3839
  craft 3839 x66
  craft 8786 until 170

step Tailoring recipes at 170
  tip Still at the Expert trainer: Black Mageweave Vest (from 170).
  learn 12048 npc 1346 only Alliance
  learn 12048 npc 4576 only Horde

step Black Mageweave Vest to 200
  tip Black Mageweave Vest is orange at 170 (yellow 185, green 200, grey 215): about 36 crafts to 200, up to 40 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Bolt of Mageweave and 3 Silken Thread. Make the 72 Bolt of Mageweave first. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data.
  craft 3865 x72
  craft 12048 until 200

step Tailoring recipes at 200
  tip Black Mageweave Headband (from 200) is taught only by the Artisan trainers: Alliance Timothy Worthington (Dustwallow Marsh); Horde Daryl Stack (Hillsbrad Foothills). You can train Artisan there now if you are level 35 (it needs Tailoring 200), which saves the trip at 225.
  learn 12072 npc 11052 only Alliance
  learn 12072 npc 2399 only Horde map 1424
  train Tailoring Artisan optional

step Black Mageweave Headband to 225
  tip Black Mageweave Headband is orange at 200 (yellow 205, green 220, grey 235): about 37 crafts to 225, up to 44 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 3 Bolt of Mageweave and 2 Heavy Silken Thread. Make the 111 Bolt of Mageweave first. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Tailoring 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3865 x111
  craft 12072 until 225
  skill Tailoring 225

